# viavitae-brand .gitignore
# Node + Python + OS + export artefacts. Trimmed from the viavitae-template
# superset: this repository holds no infrastructure, so the Terraform and state
# sections are gone, and it holds no application, so the framework caches that
# never appear here are gone too.
#
# Never un-ignore a secret, key or environment file. If a value must be
# committed, it is not a secret and belongs in documentation or a schema.
#
# The governing rule for this file is one line: SOURCES ARE COMMITTED, DERIVED
# ARTEFACTS ARE NOT. An SVG master is a source. A PNG rasterised from it is
# derived. A committed derived artefact is a second copy of a value that can
# disagree with the first, and the disagreement is always found by a consumer
# downloading the stale one rather than by a reviewer. tools/build_exports.py
# regenerates everything ignored below, and .github/workflows/ci.yml uploads it.

# --- Secrets and credentials -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
secrets/
.secrets.baseline
# Terraform state files can contain credentials in plaintext. This repository
# holds no infrastructure, but the compliance governance check requires every
# repository to ignore state patterns so a stray .tfstate is never committed.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# --- Python (tools/) ---------------------------------------------------------
# The scripts under tools/ are linted and type-checked in CI, so their caches
# are local and never committed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage/
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
junit.xml
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/
.cache/

# Python's own `build/` directory is NOT ignored here, and that is a deliberate
# departure from the template this file was trimmed from. In this repository
# build/ is committed source: build/tailwind.preset.ts is the web consumption
# entry point and build/css/tokens.css is what a consumer imports. A blanket
# `build/` pattern would silently un-track the entire distribution surface of the
# brand system. Only `dist/` — which nothing here writes — is kept.
dist/

# --- Node (build/package.json, examples/nextjs) ------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.turbo/
.npm/
.yarn/
.pnp.*
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
.parcel-cache/
.vite/

# No lockfile is committed for build/package.json, because its only
# devDependencies are a formatter and a type-checker pinned to exact versions
# and the package is never installed as an application. If that changes — if a
# real dependency graph appears — commit the lockfile and switch CI from
# `npm install --no-package-lock` to `npm ci` in the same pull request.

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# --- Export artefacts: every raster derived from an SVG master ---------------
# Each file below is produced by `python3 tools/build_exports.py` and uploaded as
# a workflow artefact by .github/workflows/ci.yml. The SVG masters ARE committed
# and are the only source; a committed PNG would be a second copy of the mark
# that can disagree with the first, and the disagreement is found by whoever
# downloads the stale one. Each output directory keeps a committed README.md
# naming every file that lands in it and the command that produces it, so a
# contributor who clones the repository is not left looking at an empty folder
# wondering whether a build failed. That README is why the two raster-exports
# patterns below ignore the directory CONTENTS with a trailing /* rather than the
# directory itself with a trailing /: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so `png/` would swallow its own README and a following
# `!png/README.md` would silently do nothing. tools/build_exports.py asserts each
# README is present, which is the only check that would have caught this.
assets/logo/raster-exports/png/*
!assets/logo/raster-exports/png/README.md
assets/logo/raster-exports/webp/*
!assets/logo/raster-exports/webp/README.md
assets/favicon/*.png
assets/favicon/*.ico
assets/og/og-default.png
assets/social/avatar-400.png

# Liturgical photography is NOT ignored. It is a committed brand asset library
# with a per-file licence record in assets/imagery/liturgical/README.md, and a
# licence record that points at a file which is not in the repository is not a
# licence record. Keep individual files under 2MB and prefer WebP; a full-resolution
# archive belongs in object storage, not in git history, where it is retained
# forever by every clone whether or not anyone still needs it.

# Font binaries. Both families are SIL Open Font Licensed and may be
# redistributed, but a variable font is several hundred kilobytes and the shipped
# subset is derived from it, so neither belongs here. Fetch from the family's own
# release page into assets/typography/self-hosted-woff2/ and run
# `python3 tools/build_exports.py --fonts`. The OFL licence text and the README in
# each family directory ARE committed: those are the compliance record, and the
# compliance record is the part that has to survive.
*.ttf
*.otf
*.woff
*.woff2
.*.instanced.ttf

# --- Editors and IDEs --------------------------------------------------------
.idea/*
!.idea/runConfigurations/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.classpath
.settings/

# --- Operating systems -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Archives ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.rar
*.7z
*.dmg
*.iso

# --- Local staging directories and scratch venvs -----------------------------
# These are temporary staging areas for generation runs targeting sibling repos.
# They must never be committed. Delete after migration.
/.api-staging/
/.demos-staging/
/.infra-staging/
/.api-verify-venv/
/.infra-verify-venv/
/.infra-tools/
/.qoder/
/.viavitae-*-spec.md
